.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1204 PM PDT Sat Sep 26 2026
(Monday through next Friday)

Ridging should return to the region on Monday as the low moves into
the Mojave Desert, setting up pushes of higher elevation offshore
flow each morning from Monday to Wednesday, chiefly across the North
and East Bay interior mountains. The strongest push looks to be on
Tuesday morning with wind gusts of 25 to 35 mph possible in the
interior mountains of the North Bay. The potential for wind gusts
above 35 mph is greatest at the ridgeline of the Vaca Mountains
along the eastern border of Napa County.

Otherwise, the arrival of the ridge should allow for temperatures to
warm for the next week. By Tuesday, highs should reach the middle
80s to middle 90s in the inland valleys, the middle 70s to the
middle 80s for the Bayshore regions, and the 60s to the lower 70s
for the Pacific coast. These highs should basically remain stable
through the rest of the 7-day outlook as ensemble model means and
cluster guidance suggest that the ridging pattern should stick
around in some shape or form into the upcoming weekend and possibly
beyond.

