.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1046 AM PDT Sat Sep 26 2026

Stratus is clearing rapidly across affected area terminal at this
hour. VFR conditions expected prevail through this afternoon with
a return of low clouds expected this evening over coastal
terminals (KMRY and KHAF) and after midnight/early Sunday morning
over inland terminals.

A short wave trough approaching the region tonight into Sunday
will deepens the marine layer overnight. This may result in light
rain or drizzle especially along the coast. However the
relatively dry boundary layer may not allow it to reach the ground
and may result in virga.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR conditions with scattered high clouds will
prevail through the remainder of the day with moderate confidence
that MVFR cigs will return overnight. Lighter winds than yesterday
are anticipated. An approaching short wave trough will deepens
the marine layer overnight resulting in the possibility of wet
runways by morning due to light rain or drizzle.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to KSFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR conditions will prevail through the
remainder of the day with moderately high confidence that MVFR
cigs will return this evening. Light to locally moderate onshore
flow is anticipated. An approaching short wave trough will
deepens the marine layer overnight resulting in the possibility
of wet runways by morning due to light rain or drizzle.

